  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -8 & 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -8 & 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot columns are the $2$nd and $5$th columns.",
